celerate the development of robust technical safety solutions. Systemic risks, which can propagate across interconnected systems and societies, demand a collective, multi-stakeholder response that transcends individual organizational capacities. No single lab possesses the full spectrum of expertise or resources to unilaterally mitigate all potential existential risks or develop comprehensive technical approaches to AI safety, such as robust interpretability tools or scalable oversight methods. Sharing research pools diverse methodologies, accelerates the development of standardized frontier safety frameworks and risk tiers, and allows for rapid identification and dissemination of best practices across the entire AI ecosystem. Therefore, an open, collaborative approach to safety research fundamentally strengthens our collective ability to manage and mitigate AI's most profound challenges.",
